            <ArticleTitle>Solitary plasmacytoma of the skull base.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>665-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Plasmacytomas involving the skull base are rare lesions that may be well advanced by the time of diagnosis. Because of their anatomic site they may produce a variety of signs and symptoms, some of which may be vague, often resulting in delays in presentation and in appropriate investigations. We present such a patient, discuss the diagnosis and management, and give a review of the literature.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
